        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1aa5c06f-4d52-53fd-be19-6940042af9de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wernher von Braun, Walter Dornberger\n- Events: Operation Lighthouse\n- Projects: Aggregate 3\n- Places: Greifswalder Oie\n- Roles: German Army artillery officer, Major-General\n- Topics: World War I, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Walter Dornberger was born on 6 September 1895.\n- Walter Dornberger was a German Army artillery officer, and his career spanned World War I and World War II.\n- In December 1937, Wernher von Braun and Walter Dornberger carried out Operation Lighthouse on the German island of Greifswalder Oie.\n- Operation Lighthouse was the name given to a failed experimental launch of four Aggregate 3 liquid-fuel rockets.\n- Walter Robert Dornberger held the rank of Major-General and had the title Dr.\n- Walter Dornberger died on 27 June 1980.",
